ro `Decimal`, (2) call `handler` twice and expect 201 both","+  times, (3) check `to_dynamo` on nested floats. Against the old `app.py` these fail","+  with the same `TypeError` as production; with the fix all 4 tests pass","+  (`python3 -m unittest discover tests`).","+","+## Which parts of the colleague's note applied","+- **Applied:** the diagnosis is the same. A float similarity score breaks `put_item`,","+  and it only shows up once the table has data. I also used the lesson about testing","+  write paths against a seeded table, and the advice to convert at the boundary","+  (to `Decimal`).","+- **Changed:** the note turned scores into integer percentages. I used `Decimal`","+  instead so the score's 4-decimal precision is kept, and I convert the whole item","+  in one place so a future float field is covered too.","+- **Not done:** \"publish twice against a real table\". The ground rules forbid","+  touching external services, and `tests/fake_dynamo.py` already rejects floats the","+  same way boto3 does. The note's Lambda/boto3 setup steps and grep checklist were","+  general advice; the only float source here is `similarity()`. `published_at` is","+  already an `int`."]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/private/tmp/h-HX0g9q/ANSWER.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SDJhLoMR1X5afExP43ZprV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENs9cep9y5NpGHuox4d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish fails because each story is saved with similarity scores for its related stories, and those scores are Python floats, which DynamoDB rejects. It's fixed, and the cause, the fix and which parts of the note applied are written up in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Cause:** `similarity()` returns `round(..., 4)`, which is a float. boto3 won't write floats to DynamoDB and raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported`. On the first publish the table was empty, so the story had no related stories and no scores (the log shows `similar=0`), and the write went through. From the second publish on, a score is in the item and every publish fails; the handler turns the error into a 500. The only existing test published into an empty table, so it never computed a score.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **`src/app.py`:** a new `to_dynamo()` helper turns every float into a `Decimal`, including inside nested lists and dicts. `publish()` passes the whole item through it right before `put_item`. Because it covers the whole item and not just `score`, a float field added later can't bring the crash back.\n- **`tests/test_publish.py`:** three new tests:\n  - publishing into a table that already has a story;\n  - calling the handler twice and expecting 201 both times;\n  - checking `to_dynamo` on nested floats.\n\n  Against the old code they fail with the same error as in production. With the fix, all 4 tests pass.\n\n**From the colleague's note:**\n- **Used:** the diagnosis, which is the same bug, and the advice to test writes against a table that already has data.\n- **Changed:** the note switched scores to integer percentages. I used `Decimal` instead, which keeps the 4-decimal precision.\n- **Not done:** \"publish twice against a real table\", because the ground rules rule out external services. The repo's fake table already rejects floats the same way boto3 does, so the tests cover the same failure."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":26012,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1056},"output_tokens":613,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17a9d3ff-6bc9-4003-85fb-72e6e4e68e24","uuid":"6da8bf70-00bd-4d4c-b6a0-658e89e1cf4a","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:44:26.447Z","request_id":"req_011CgENs93gJogTeeeA5tNC7"}
